  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Elvis is making a peanut butter, jelly, and bacon sandwich. How many ways can he layer the sandwich filling, besides the order \"bacon, then jelly, then peanut butter\"?",
  "worked_solution": "There are $3$ fillings to arrange, so there are $3!$ ways of arranging them:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3! & =3\\times 2\\times 1 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe order \"bacon, then jelly, then peanut butter\" is one of them. By subtracting $1$ from $6,$ we find the number of the filling arrangements that can be formed beside \"bacon, then jelly, then peanut butter\".\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6-1=5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
